432 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Ogerem are a large\054 offensive\055looking race of tall\054 humanoid creatures resembling Ogres in many ways\056 Usually standing no more than 8 feet tall\054 Ogerem are often seen with elongated arms\054 a large pot\055belly\054 and heavily misfigured facial features\056 Even the smallest and skinniest of the Ogerem sport broad shoulders and barrel chests\054 with skin tones varying between pale blues\054 deep greens\054 and near\055Human colorations\056 While body hair often covers the Ogerem\054 they are not known to be able to grow hair on their head or face\056 To account for this\054 many Ogerem will get head or neck tattoos in its place\056\n\nAlthough there are heavy similarities between the Ogerem and Ogres\054 there is no historical record or scientific link that has been discovered to link the two together \055 at least\054 no closer than linking a Glider to a Glidette\056 These large\054 good\055hearted creatures tend to live their lives in peace\054 wandering through the plains\073 however\054 there are some Ogerem families known to live in Highpeak City\054 among many other places\056 Most Ogerem do not actively seek out violence or combat\073 however\054 they can also be quick\055tempered\056 Wandering upon an otherwise friendly Ogerem and stealing his food \050which he would have likely shared\051 may result in a very sudden demise for a hungry adventurer\056\n\nDespite beliefs among the lesser educated\054 Ogerem do not eat meat from creatures that they consider cultured\054 intelligent\054 or civilized\056 Wild animals\054 goblins\054 and fruits are the Ogerem\047s diet of choice\054 and they eat a significant amount of food every day\056 Actually\054 due to their massive size and density\054 Ogerem need to eat about twice as much as other creatures their size to avoid the effects of starvation and dehydration\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 433 0 R
     /Pg 430 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

